Method of part 2
- One runner outside the repository: /tmp/opencode/p3b-mut/run.py. A copy sits in this folder as
  jr-green-p3b-book-mutants-run.py.
- Each mutant: copy the target file to /tmp/opencode/p3b-mut/backup, apply one exact string
  replacement, and assert that the old string occurs exactly one time. Then run
  npx vitest run TESTFILE --maxWorkers=1 --bail=1 from dashboard with CI=true. Caught when the exit
  code is not 0. Then restore from the copy and compare with cmp.
- The pre-flight git status of dashboard/lib/storytime and dashboard/scripts/storytime was empty.
- Every run went through heavy-run.sh with HEAVY_MIN_AVAIL_MB=1500 and
  HEAVY_PREFLIGHT_WAIT_S=5400. One heavy run for MB and one for MX.
- All 37 snippets fit the code one time. No mutant was recorded as n/a.

